### Describe the bug

`BeanAsArrayBuilderDeserializer._deserializeNonVanilla()` ignores the value returned by `SettableBeanProperty.deserializeSetAndReturn()`:

```java
if (activeView == null || prop.visibleInView(activeView)) {
    try {
        prop.deserializeSetAndReturn(p, ctxt, builder);   // return value dropped
```

For a Builder whose `withXxx()` methods return a new instance (immutable builder), every value set in this loop is lost, and `build()` is called on the original, empty builder. The vanilla path (`deserialize()`) and `_deserializeFromNonArray()` correctly use `builder = prop.deserializeSetAndReturn(...)`; so do all the loops in `BuilderBasedDeserializer`.

`_deserializeNonVanilla()` is used for `@JsonFormat(shape = ARRAY)` builders whenever vanilla processing is not possible: for example, with an active view (`readerWithView()`) when the builder has views, or with injectables.

### Version Information

All active branches: 2.18, 2.21, 2.x, 3.1, 3.2, 3.x (same code at `BeanAsArrayBuilderDeserializer.java:230` in 3.x, `:234` in 2.x).

### Reproduction

```java
@JsonDeserialize(builder = Value.Builder.class)
@JsonFormat(shape = JsonFormat.Shape.ARRAY)
static class Value {
    final int x, y;
    Value(int x, int y) { this.x = x; this.y = y; }

    @JsonPropertyOrder({ "x", "y" })
    @JsonFormat(shape = JsonFormat.Shape.ARRAY)
    static class Builder {
        final int x, y;
        Builder() { this(0, 0); }
        Builder(int x, int y) { this.x = x; this.y = y; }

        @JsonView(Object.class)
        public Builder withX(int v) { return new Builder(v, y); }
        @JsonView(Object.class)
        public Builder withY(int v) { return new Builder(x, v); }

        public Value build() { return new Value(x, y); }
    }
}

ObjectMapper m = JsonMapper.builder().build();
Value v = m.readValue("[1,2]", Value.class);
// x=1, y=2: correct (vanilla path)
v = m.readerWithView(Object.class).forType(Value.class).readValue("[1,2]");
// x=0, y=0: values lost (non-vanilla path)
```

Verified on 3.3.0-SNAPSHOT.

### Expected behavior

`[1,2]` read with an active view that includes both properties should produce `x=1, y=2`, same as without a view.

### Additional context

Fix is a one-liner: `builder = prop.deserializeSetAndReturn(p, ctxt, builder);`. Found during review of #6224 (#6219).

