### Describe the issue

`BeanPropertyMap.withProperty()` has an "in-place" branch: if a property with the same name already exists, it overwrites `_propsInOrder[i]` on `this` and returns `this`, instead of returning a copy.

`BeanDeserializerBase.withObjectIdReader()` calls `src._beanProperties.withProperty(idProp)`, so when the `ObjectIdValueProperty` name matches an existing property (always the case with `ObjectIdGenerators.PropertyGenerator`), the `BeanPropertyMap` of the *source* (cached, non-contextual) deserializer gets modified. As a result, Object Id handling leaks into all other uses of the value type with the same mapper.

### Version

