Found during review of #6317.

`@JsonFormat(shape = ARRAY)` deserialization spins forever if the token stream ends before the closing `END_ARRAY` and there are extra values to skip. The loops only stop on `END_ARRAY`. At end of input `nextToken()` returns `null`, `skipChildren()` does nothing, and the thread never exits the loop.

JSON text parsers are not affected because they throw at end of input. It takes a parser that returns `null` instead, such as `TokenBuffer` (#6376 covers the same kind of input for Object properties).

## Reproduction

With `FAIL_ON_UNKNOWN_PROPERTIES` disabled:

```java
@JsonFormat(shape = JsonFormat.Shape.ARRAY)
@JsonPropertyOrder({ "x" })
static class P { public int x; }

ObjectReader r = JsonMapper.builder()
        .disable(DeserializationFeature.FAIL_ON_UNKNOWN_PROPERTIES)
        .build()
        .readerFor(P.class);
try (TokenBuffer tb = TokenBuffer.forGeneration()) {
    tb.writeStartArray();
    tb.writeNumber(1);
    tb.writeNumber(2);
    // no writeEndArray()
    r.readValue(tb.asParser()); // never returns
}
```

